Cell[TextData[{
 "We could follow the ",
 StyleBox["\[RightSkeleton]",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 " to see what ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " can tell us about the properties of the unfamiliar functions to which the \
physics of simple pendula has unexpectedly led us. Or we might consult the \
mathematical handbooks  (see, ",
 StyleBox["e.g",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "., J. Spanier & K. B. Oldham, ",
 StyleBox["An Atlas of Functions",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (1987), page 637). We will see how far we can go without making such an \
effort\[LongDash]trusting to ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 StyleBox["'s",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " knowledge of the subject. Noting that the solutions presented above differ \
only in sign, we write"
}], "Text",
